{"agent":"impl-lane-interface","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"Given an environment where the built-in module `ddflow.services.lane_headless` cannot be imported (for example, an optional dependency it pulls in is missing, or a partial install lacks the module), `driver_for(\"process-headless\")` calls `importlib.import_module(\"ddflow.services.lane_headless\")` and lets the resulting `ImportError` propagate. The function is annotated `Lane | Result` and documented as returning an `unavailable` Result when it cannot provide the transport, and the stated intent is that a missing capability is reported unavailable; instead the caller crashes with an exception.","digest":"8808bf73334d4df3","location":"ddflow/services/lane_driver.py:driver_for","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lane_driver.py:driver_for"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"If an optional string parameter is `None` instead of the empty string—common when a config field has no value—`spec_from_headless` treats it as a real value. For example, with a descriptor whose `model_flag` is `\"--model\"`, `spec_from_headless(\"lane\", headless, model=None)` passes the `val != \"\"` test, stores `values[\"model\"] = str(None) == \"None\"`, and appends `--model {model}`; the lane is launched with the literal model name `None` rather than leaving the model unset. The same happens for `effort`, `mcp_config`, and `session`; a `session=None` with a resume flag becomes a resume session id of `\"None\"`, guessing a value instead of reporting absence.","digest":"0cad53bfaa39b817","location":"ddflow/services/lane_driver.py:spec_from_headless","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lane_driver.py:spec_from_headless"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The child environment is built by setting `HOME` (and `home_env`) to the lane-private home and then applying `spec.fixed_env` and `r.env` afterwards. Given `LaunchSpec(fixed_env={\"HOME\": \"[REDACTED:path]\"})`, or a rendered `r.env` containing `HOME`, the final child `HOME` is the non-private value, not the lane-private directory. The driver then removes only the private directory it created, so the agent can read/write config under the user’s real home and the cleanup/isolation contract is broken.","digest":"5db2b99b84974e33","location":"ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:_prepare","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:_prepare"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"Prompt delivery is keyed on the wrong signal: `_prepare` only writes `prompt.txt` when `\"{prompt_file}\"` is an exact argv element, while `start` later decides whether to write stdin based on `\"prompt_file\" in values`. If a caller supplies `spec.values={\"prompt_file\": \"/tmp/stale\"}` while using `spec.argv=[\"agent\"]` and `spec.prompt=\"secret\"`, `_prepare` never creates the prompt file, but `start` sees `prompt_file` in `values`, skips the stdin writer, and closes stdin. The prompt is silently dropped. The same proxy also fails for templates that embed the placeholder inside an argv token, e.g. `--prompt-file={prompt_file}`.","digest":"79afacfdc92834e6","location":"ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:_prepare/start","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:_prepare/start"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"When `spec.home` is supplied, `_prepare` may create `prompt.txt` inside that directory, but the directory is not added to `private`, and `_cleanup` only removes `private`. For example, with `spec.home=Path(\"/tmp/lane-home\")`, `spec.argv=[\"agent\", \"{prompt_file}\"]`, and `spec.prompt=\"secret\"`, the driver writes `/tmp/lane-home/prompt.txt`; after `stop()` or a post-exit `status()`, that prompt file remains. The driver-created prompt is not cleaned up even when the launch later fails before spawn.","digest":"2c42160fea5a61bb","location":"ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:_prepare/_cleanup","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:_prepare/_cleanup"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`status()` calls `_cleanup()` as soon as the leader process has an exit code, without stopping the process group. If the headless agent forks a background worker in the same process group and then exits, `status()` sees the leader exit and removes the lane-private home while the worker is still running. On Unix this deletes the home directory out from under the surviving process, violating the stated cleanup-by-process-group behavior and causing later file creation or agent state writes to fail.","digest":"08e3720f23dc16c8","location":"ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:status","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:status"},{"chunk":5,"detail":"`--echo-env` and `--pwd-home` construct JSON with `%` interpolation instead of `json.dumps`, so environment values containing `\"` or `\\` (or control characters) emit invalid JSON. For example, with `HOME=C:\\Users\\test` on Windows, `--pwd-home` prints `{\"type\":\"home\",\"home\":\"C:\\Users\\test\"}`; the backslashes are invalid JSON escapes, so a driver parsing stdout treats the line as noise and the lane-private home telemetry assertion fails. The same occurs on any platform with an env value containing a double quote.","digest":"35749bbb98ff4b53","location":"tests/fixtures/lane_driver/fake_agent.py:38","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/fixtures/lane_driver/fake_agent.py:38"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The test waits only for `pidfile.exists()` and then immediately does `child = int(pidfile.read_text())`. File existence does not guarantee that the file contains a complete PID. If `fake_agent.py` writes the child PID with the usual non-atomic `open(..., \"w\")` / `Path.write_text(...)` sequence, the test can observe the file after truncation but before the full write, or after a partial write. For example, if the real child PID is `12345` and the test reads `12`, it then waits for PID `12` (often an unrelated long-lived process) and fails with “the grandchild outlived the group kill”; if it reads an empty file, `int()` raises `ValueError`. This makes the test intermittently fail even when the driver correctly killed the process group.","digest":"d9214dc9c1a0a94d","location":"tests/test_lane_driver.py:test_stop_kills_the_whole_process_group_and_removes_home","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_lane_driver.py:test_stop_kills_the_whole_process_group_and_removes_home"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The test named `..._writes_a_private_file` never inspects the prompt file: it only asserts that `start` did not return a `Result` and that the lane finishes. If the driver writes a prompt file with the wrong content, with permissive permissions such as `0644`, or fails to clean it up, the test still passes. It can therefore pass while violating the “private file” contract the test is supposed to enforce.","digest":"e11b2a3743e108fb","location":"tests/test_lane_driver.py:test_prompt_file_placeholder_writes_a_private_file","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_lane_driver.py:test_prompt_file_placeholder_writes_a_private_file"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":40921,"diff_sha":"781fa6ec1d01f366b616c0747403a568968884fcbef86e1e0d13b3744e59108e","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":622.8,"excluded_bytes":6625,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":9,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"b0cf9cb9545c4c7b","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DRV-lane-interface.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261030T154948Z-36ac9838.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewed_head":"1c794dbf673f0a957ade21d98986ef7ea0baa30b","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 e117077e46542d60c9dc9df6db3ea731d0779b13","ddflow/config_sections/lanes.py":"100644 4f78bc4278a503a0d50e69081ffe0aa12b1bedbb","ddflow/services/lane_driver.py":"100644 6a3193c25661dac0eacd7940a2643b9dc0c0a5b2","ddflow/services/lane_headless.py":"100644 32fc165fca151a25d1c9a84e8a281ca50da44f19","docs/ddflow/lane-driver.md":"100644 f1b4c5ade5397b157ab2c9627abd2f66929fc896","tests/fixtures/lane_driver/fake_agent.py":"100644 91b1ad5d56ce65b1d6a8596b99b6fa641fed5b6f","tests/fixtures/lane_driver/limit.jsonl":"100644 f6a1cecfb7e83c18dd75eeb1de1bde9426323430","tests/fixtures/lane_driver/ok.jsonl":"100644 94877f7bd05698ba1d756c662c61e2d53d43db8d","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_outputs.ambr":"100644 f10458b426113cc1d2c4207d8c92d12599c37f7f","tests/test_lane_driver.py":"100644 318453619f7c5a1a8018156f43cf6922dda35087"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/lane_driver.py:driver_for","ddflow/services/lane_driver.py:spec_from_headless","ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:_prepare","ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:_prepare/start","ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:_prepare/_cleanup","ddflow/services/lane_headless.py:status","tests/fixtures/lane_driver/fake_agent.py:38","tests/test_lane_driver.py:test_stop_kills_the_whole_process_group_and_removes_home","tests/test_lane_driver.py:test_prompt_file_placeholder_writes_a_private_file"],"tree_sha":"7b437538d07f+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":2},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"9 finding(s)"},"id":"ec1f325f9513a313f22b410c9","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":114988,"schema":1,"subject":"DRV-lane-interface","ts":"2026-10-30T16:34:21.824401Z"}
